hor_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Neovim version (nvim -v)\r\n\r\nc632f64e247c672e425f609bb47a9ab0517a4c31\r\n\r\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\r\n\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n### Operating system/version\r\n\r\nmacOS 12.1\r\n\r\n### Terminal name/version\r\n\r\niTerm 3.4.15\r\n\r\n### $TERM environment variable\r\n\r\ntmux-256color\r\n\r\n### Installation\r\n\r\nbrew install --HEAD neovim\r\n\r\n### How to reproduce the issue\r\n\r\n1. `nvim --clean`\r\n2. Source the [example code for user command previews](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/c632f64e247c672e425f609bb47a9ab0517a4c31/runtime/doc/map.txt#L1468-L1533), which creates a user command `:TrimTrailingWhitespace`.\r\n3. Define a new user command `:TrimWhitespace` with `command TrimWhitespace echo \"foobarbaz\"`.\r\n4. Start typing `:Trim` in the Vim command-line.\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nNeovim does not segfault. A custom preview is not shown until the typed command is disambiguated.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nNeovim segfaults.\r\n\r\nI think this is because we are missing a NULL check [here](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/c632f64e247c672e425f609bb47a9ab0517a4c31/src/nvim/ex_docmd.c#L10136). `find_ex_command` states that [it will return `NULL` for an ambiguous user command](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/c632f64e247c672e425f609bb47a9ab0517a4c31/src/nvim/ex_docmd.c#L2946). :Slig","closed_by":{"login":"zeertzjq","id":35768171,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NzY4MTcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35768171?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeertzjq","html_url":"https://github.com/zeertzjq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeertzjq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeertzjq/following{/other_user}","gists_url